pibridge (2.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The Monado backend is back, as PiBridge's own Monado fork in the source
    tree (third_party/monado), now packaged as pibridge-monado under
    /usr/lib/pibridge/monado (cap_sys_nice set at install). One "VR backend"
    choice in the Dashboard's top bar also points the system's OpenXR runtime
    (active_runtime.json) at SteamVR or Monado.
  * PiBridge World: the Monado backend's home in the headset, a Godot 4
    project, shipped exported into one executable (pibridge-world): no
    Godot needed. From source, pibridge-get-godot fetches the official
    Godot 4.7.2 and checks it against its published checksum.
  * The packaged app looks only in the user's folders and /usr, never in
    the development folders (PIBRIDGE_DEV_PATHS=OFF).
  * Monado + Lighthouse: Valve Index controllers (left system button = menu,
    right one held = recenter), controllers switched on or off during the
    session (hand slots), base stations drawn in VR (optional) and in the
    room setup, the builder pinned to the tracking mode.
  * Monado inside-out: controllers the cameras do not see are hidden, not
    left hanging in the air.
  * Packages: pibridge-monado (the Monado fork); pibridge installs the
    Crystal Super's WirePlumber rule and depends on wireplumber and
    pulseaudio-utils.
  * Volume buttons on Monado for the Crystal Super, with a volume indicator
    in the in-headset overlay (pibridge-xroverlay).
  * The original Crystal (P3B) on Monado: its own inside-out (poses from
    pibridge-keepalived), its Lighthouse module, volume, power and the
    Lighthouse / inside-out switch during a session. Not yet tried on the
    headset.

 -- Albert Valiev <artscout@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:59:26 +0100

pibridge (2.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Inside-out tracking of the Crystal Super / Dream Air without Monado:
    pibridge-headtrack runs Pimax's own engine (winbridge) or Basalt and hands
    the head and controller poses to CustomHeadsetOpenVR, like the original
    Crystal's own tracking. Controllers by Pimax's LED engine with Pimax's
    25 ms prediction and the controller angle; game vibration through an
    abstract Unix socket; camera auto exposure; room anchor and recenter.
  * The original Pimax Crystal (P3B) fully supported: Lighthouse and its own
    inside-out, 72/90/120 Hz, eye tracking, sound over DisplayPort.
  * Monado is no longer built, shipped or used (no bundled SteamVR driver, no
    ONNX Runtime); the Development and Device pages are gone.
  * Dashboard: controllers with PAIR (a guided window) / UNPAIR / VIBRATE and
    their own serials, the headset's and the optical module's serials, a Sound
    card with headset sound / microphone switches, the eye calibration import.
  * Help opens the user guide inside the app.
  * EDID override for every Pimax headset (scripts, manual and EDID data).

 -- Albert Valiev <artscout@gmail.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:48:31 +0200

pibridge (1.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Crystal Super lens profiles fixed: each eye's axis is now set by a true
    rotation. "Crystal Super Oled native" (the Pimax compositor geometry) gives
    the right world scale and straight lines on head turns; "Crystal Super
    Oled chovr" keeps CustomHeadsetOpenVR's lens shape with the same axis.
    The "Like Pimax" profile is gone. The lens profile moved to the Display
    page; an explicit rec_lens_conf now says that it overrides the profile.
  * IPD on the Dashboard (Quick settings): 58-72 mm in 0.5 mm steps. It moves
    the Crystal Super's lens motors (the IPD motor command of the Pimax client,
    now allowed) and the renderers use the same value, live: Monado through
    pibridge.conf, CustomHeadsetOpenVR through its settings.json. At start the
    slider shows where the lenses are (read back from the headset). The old
    "IPD horizontal offset" is gone.
  * Headset sound: the volume is kept across switches and USB re-enumerations
    (no more 100 % after every switch), and the headset's volume buttons work
    (1 % steps, repeat while held) in Lighthouse and inside-out.
  * Import calibration from Windows moved to the Development page.
  * pibridge-build-winbridge is now installed (postinst and the docs named it,
    the package did not have it); INSTALL.md explains winbridge for package
    users (build once, never started by hand: the app runs it).
  * Windows headset data kit: reads the Pimax client settings, records IPD
    values and the headset's volume buttons. INSTALL.md points owners of other
    Pimax headsets to it.

 -- Albert Valiev <artscout@gmail.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200

pibridge (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Eye tracking now starts under SteamVR + Monado (inside-out / SLAM): the
    Play start no longer waits for pibridge-eyed to "pause" (it keeps the eye
    chip to feed the gaze shared memory), so Start VR with eye tracking on
    comes up instead of timing out.
  * Video recording captures the submitted per-eye image the headset shows,
    not the game's intermediate multiview passes: fixes mostly-black / flashing
    recordings in multi-pass games (e.g. Falcon BMS). Native and Proton games.
  * In-VR overlay: one START/STOP RECORDING button that follows the app's real
    recording state (no longer stuck "recording" after a crash); the recording
    settings (view / fps / size) live only in the app's Recording page.

 -- Albert Valiev <artscout@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0200

pibridge (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging: single .deb, prefix /usr.
    - PiBridge Qt 6 app and engine binaries, device descriptions, systemd user
      units (in /usr/lib/systemd/user), desktop entry and icons, docs.
    - Vulkan video-capture record layer (.so in /usr/lib/<triplet>/pibridge,
      implicit-layer manifest in /usr/share/vulkan/implicit_layer.d).
    - Bundled prebuilt PiBridge Monado SteamVR driver (NOT monado-service) and
      the ONNX Runtime it links; OpenCV, Qt 6, Vulkan, ffmpeg from system.
    - winbridge shipped as source + pibridge-build-winbridge helper.
    - udev rule activated from postinst; per-user setup done by the app.

 -- Albert Valiev <artscout@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:41:18 +0200
